# Working artifacts from the test-suite audit, deliberately untracked.
#
# `tests/server/file-io/roundtrip-repo-metric.test.ts` round-trips EVERY tracked
# `.md` in the repo through the Y.Doc markdown loader inside a `beforeAll` with a
# 120s budget. Committing the full audit added 20,332 markdown lines -- a 20%
# inflation of that corpus -- which took the hook from comfortably green to 68s
# in isolation and past 120s under full-suite parallel load. The fidelity
# assertions all still passed; the time budget was what broke.
#
# So the per-test evidence stays local. What IS tracked is the audit chain a
# reader needs: the report, the heat map, the production model, the cleared
# plan, the proposal inventory, the four adversarial reviews, the baseline, and
# the standard applied.
#
# To regenerate the untracked half, re-run the audit -- it is reproducible from
# `auditor-brief.md` plus the batch list in the report.

audit-parts/
model-parts/

# Machine artifacts: raw reporter output and mechanical scans.
baseline.json
test-imports.json
suite-inventory.csv
batches.txt
*.out
